7	 * The single definition of an owner's {@code householdId}: a deterministic identifier derived from
8	 * the owner's last name and postcode, so owners with the same last name and postcode share it
9	 * automatically. The value is the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over
10	 * {@code normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode}, where the last name is compared case-insensitively
11	 * after collapsing runs of whitespace.
12	 *
13	 * <p>Because it is a pure function of {@code (lastName, postcode)}, every owner computes its own id
14	 * independently and members of one household always agree — there is nothing to link or backfill.
15	 * Shared by {@link AssignHousehold} (which stamps it onto the new owner) and {@link OwnerHousehold}
16	 * (which counts household members and caps membershipLevel), so every place that keys off the household
17	 * applies the one rule and they cannot drift apart. Duplicate detection and the soft match no longer
18	 * key off the household id — they use the {@link IdentityKey} and {@link Soundex} of the last name.
19	 *
20	 * <p>Kept out of the function classes themselves because OfficeFloor requires each function class to
21	 * expose exactly one public method.
22	 */
